==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɹɛnɪt/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɛnɪt|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|renet}}, a variant of {{m|enm|renelesse}}, {{m|enm|renels}}, {{m|enm|renlys}}, {{m|enm|rendlys|t=rennet}}, from {{m|enm|rennen|t=to run}}, from {{der|en|ang|rennan}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*rannijaną}}. Compare {{cog|dum|rinsel}}, {{m|dum|runsel|t=rennet}}, {{cog|ang|ġerennan|t=to coagulate}}, {{cog|de|gerinnen|t=to coagulate; congeal}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|runnet}} {{qualifier|dialectal}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}
{{wikipedia}}

# An [[enzyme]] used as the first step in making [[cheese]], to [[curdle]] the milk and [[coagulate]] the [[casein]] in it, derived by soaking the fourth [[stomach]] of a milk-fed [[calf]] in [[brine]].

